# armour/shared/pauldron_flap2_r: the small FLAP pauldron on the right shoulder (flap.2; FORGE-SHOULDERS, STYLE_P2 28.3).
# overlapping rounded hide tabs: an upper flap over two lower ones whose round ends scallop the foot (TANNER'S,
# leather); matte, one shine.
# Rides the lean and the bob and lifts a pixel on wind-ups (`up`). Finish regions: R the lower tabs' ends, G the stitch at the top flap, N the shadow under the top flap, P the top flap.
# Shared by the man and the woman (D10). Generated by FORGE-SHOULDERS gen.py from shapes.py (re-run, never hand-edit
# the derived views). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
use person
role pauldron flap.2
layer armNear
anchor shoulderR
keys pauld
z 5
side R

view D key rest origin 2 2
|.ffff
|fjihf
|fgggf
|fifif
|.f.f.
regions
